<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suwon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suwon is a city about 30 kilometres south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Seoul</a> and the capital of Gyeonggi Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, with more than a million inhabitants. In the 1790s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeongjo-of-joseon">King Jeongjo</a> moved the tomb of his father there and built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hwaseong-fortress">Hwaseong Fortress</a> around a new town, which he hoped would become a second capital. Today it is an industrial and research centre and home to the headquarters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samsung">Samsung</a> Electronics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suwon.jpg" alt="Suwon" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 본인 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20121003_Suwon_vs_Seoul.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
